window.products.push({"id":107469,"name":"WR60X31522 Evaporator Fan Motor Refrigerator Part WR60X23584 WR60X28783 WR60X10141 WR60X10346 WR60X10046 WR60X10138 WR60X28784 Model A3316ABSARBB HTS1","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61bgz5ZZaES._SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Ge Evaporator Fan Motor Wr60x23584 - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers WR60X31522, AP5955766, WR60X10045, WR60X10046, WR60X10072, WR60X10138, WR60X10346, WR60X27646, AP6977246, WR60X10141. Wr60x23584 Evaporator Fan Motor is compatible with General Electric, Hotpoint appliances. Ge Wr60x23584 Motor Evap is an essential component of the refrigeration system, responsible for circulating air throughout the refrigerator and freezer compartments to maintain consistent temperatures. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the Wr60x31522 Ge Evaporator Fan Motor? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Evaporator Fan Wr60x31522 will help if your appliance is noisy, the fridge is too warm, the freezer section is too warm, or it doesn't start. Replacing the Ge Evaporator Fan Wr60x31522 is a straightforward process that can be done with basic tools. 💡 The Wr60x31522 Motor features a durable, high-quality construction and is built to last for a long time. Wr60x31522 Fan Motor has a compact size that makes it easy to install, and the Part Wr60x31522 is designed to operate quietly to avoid disturbing the household. Ge Wr60x31522 fits hundreds of models and can be installed in a few minutes. Ge Fan Motor Wr60x31522 meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 Will fridge work without evaporator fan? The refrigerator can technically operate without an evaporator fan, but it will not work efficiently. The Ge Part Wr60x31522 helps to circulate cold air throughout the refrigerator and freezer compartments, which is necessary for proper temperature regulation. Without the evaporator fan, the cold air would not circulate efficiently, and the temperature in the refrigerator and freezer would be uneven, with some areas being too cold and others too warm. 💡 How do you test an evaporator fan motor? To test the Ge Refrigerator Fan Motor Wr60x31522, locate it in the refrigerator's freezer compartment, unplug the refrigerator, remove the back panel, and disconnect the wires. Check the continuity of the wires with a multimeter, inspect the Ge Fan Motor Wr60x23584 for physical damage, and connect a power source to see if the fan blade spins. If the fan blade spins, the motor is working correctly. If it does not, the motor needs to be replaced.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61bgz5ZZaES._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B08LVWL6GF","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-107469","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08LVWL6GF","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B08LVWL6GF","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
